# W44-80 — re-test 15-cluster BlockCtxMap::default on top of main (post W44-73/W44-77/W44-78)

## Question

W44-71 (`01cde909` on origin/w44-71-wip) ported libjxl's 15-cluster simple
BlockCtxMap default but regressed 6 of 12 cells when applied on top of
W44-68 main, with 0 cells improving. W44-73 added the LZ77+ANS context-map
writer (the diagnosed binding constraint at that time). Since then,
W44-77 (cost-model audit) and W44-78 (HIGH_D_PHOTO_MIN_DISTANCE 4.0 → 3.0)
have landed.

Does the W44-71 cherry-pick on top of current main (W44-79 tip,
`2ced8d29`) close the regression?

## Method

Sibling workspace `~/work/zen/jxl-encoder--w44-80-retry-15cluster`,
jj on main, rebased onto `ktlrzvot 2ced8d29` (W44-79 tip).

1. Build CLI on clean main (commit `2ced8d29`) → baseline bytes.
2. Apply W44-71 source-only patch (4 files from `01cde909`, sans
   bench artifacts) → patched bytes.
3. Re-encode 12 F-D test cells (3 images × 4 distances) at e7,
   release build, single-thread CLI.
4. Compare bytes deltas vs each other and vs cjxl v0.12.0 (cjxl numbers
   from `benchmarks/w44_73_context_map_lz77_ans_2026-05-19.tsv`).

## Result

| image    | d | base   | patched | ΔB    | Δ%     | verdict             |
|---       |---|---     |---      |---    |---     |---                  |
| 1420710  | 3 | 36505  | 36505   |  0    |  0.00  | byte-identical      |
| 1420710  | 4 | 26702  | 26702   |  0    |  0.00  | byte-identical      |
| 1420710  | 5 | 24589  | 24751   | +162  | +0.66  | REGRESS             |
| 1420710  | 6 | 21212  | 21369   | +157  | +0.74  | REGRESS             |
| 1531677  | 3 | 32246  | 32246   |  0    |  0.00  | byte-identical      |
| 1531677  | 4 | 24367  | 24367   |  0    |  0.00  | byte-identical      |
| 1531677  | 5 | 21059  | 21270   | +211  | +1.00  | REGRESS             |
| 1531677  | 6 | 18084  | 18346   | +262  | +1.45  | REGRESS             |
| 1189261  | 3 | 30481  | 30481   |  0    |  0.00  | byte-identical      |
| 1189261  | 4 | 24380  | 24380   |  0    |  0.00  | byte-identical      |
| 1189261  | 5 | 19778  | 19811   |  +33  | +0.17  | REGRESS             |
| 1189261  | 6 | 16816  | 17065   | +249  | +1.48  | REGRESS             |

**6 of 12 regress (+33 to +262 B). 0 of 12 improve. 6 byte-identical.**

Total bytes delta: +1276 B across the 12 cells. Per-cell average: +106 B.

## Comparison to prior W44-73 run

W44-73 already ran the same 12-cell test with the same patch on top
of W44-73 (`benchmarks/w44_73_context_map_lz77_ans_2026-05-19.tsv`
rows 10-18) and observed essentially identical deltas:

- 1420710 d=6: +94 B then (21295 → 21389), +157 B now (21212 → 21369)
- 1531677 d=6: +109 B then (18227 → 18336), +262 B now (18084 → 18346)
- 1189261 d=6: -94 B then (16910 → 16816)*, +249 B now (16816 → 17065)

*W44-73's "ours_new" column was the W73 BASELINE (4-cluster, with the new
LZ77+ANS writer) — it was a -94 B win vs the W73 pre-baseline 4-cluster
Huffman+MTF writer. Adding W44-71 on top moves UP from that base by
similar +33 to +262 B amounts.

The regression magnitudes are unchanged in shape (1531677 worst, 1189261
slight). W44-78 distance-gate widening doesn't interact with the clustering
binding constraint — it only flips one cell (1420710 d=3) to a smaller
table that doesn't trigger 15-cluster gain in EITHER path.

## Decision

**Honest-stop. Do NOT cherry-pick W44-71 onto main.**

W44-73 already validated this exact combination (`w44_73_..._2026-05-19.md`
"W44-71 verdict (gate c)") and reached the same conclusion. Re-running
post-W44-78 reproduces the regression with no improvement.

Per W44-73's diagnosis: cjxl has additional levers (different pair-merge
cost model, different ANS strategy thresholds, possibly different
quantize-counts targets) that let it benefit from finer-grained context
maps. Our cluster_histograms (W44-75 bit-exact audit) and writer
(W44-73 LZ77+ANS port) are both at parity, but pair-merge / scheduling
upstream is not. Issue #59 stays open; should be re-scoped to
"investigate why cjxl's 15c works AND ours regresses with the same writer
and same clustering algorithm."

W44-71 stays parked on `origin/w44-71-wip` bookmark.

## Time spent

~45 min (workspace, two builds, two 12-cell sweeps, this writeup).

## Reproducer

```bash
jj workspace add ~/work/zen/jxl-encoder--w44-80-retry-15cluster
cd ~/work/zen/jxl-encoder--w44-80-retry-15cluster
jj rebase -d main

# Baseline build
cargo build --release -p jxl-encoder-cli
for img in 1420710 1531677 1189261; do
  for d in 3 4 5 6; do
    ./target/release/cjxl-rs -e 7 -d $d \
      /home/lilith/work/codec-corpus/CID22/CID22-512/validation/${img}.png \
      /tmp/${img}_d${d}_base.jxl
  done
done

# Cherry-pick W44-71 source diff
git -C ~/work/zen/jxl-encoder show 01cde909 -- \
  'jxl-encoder/src/jpeg/encode.rs' \
  'jxl-encoder/src/vardct/ac_context.rs' \
  'jxl-encoder/src/vardct/bitstream.rs' \
  'jxl-encoder/src/vardct/encoder.rs' > /tmp/w44_71_src.patch
patch -p1 < /tmp/w44_71_src.patch
cargo build --release -p jxl-encoder-cli
# Repeat the loop with output suffix _patched.
```

## Config grid

- Host: AMD Ryzen 9 7950X, 128 GB RAM, water-cooled.
- Toolchain: rustc 1.91.0 stable, release profile.
- jxl-encoder commit hash: `2ced8d29` (W44-79 tip on origin/main).
- W44-71 patch: `01cde909` from `origin/w44-71-wip` bookmark
  (source-only, no bench artifacts).
- CLI: `cjxl-rs -e 7 -d {3,4,5,6}` single-thread.
- Corpus: CID22-512 validation subset (3 photos).
- cjxl reference: v0.12.0 numbers from prior W44-73 sweep.

